  "text": "australasian\nSteamship\nDiners'\nHederatian.\nSTEAMSHIP BUILDINGS.\n509 COLLINS STREET.\nMelbourne,\n10th June, 1955.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nPlease accept from my Members\nof course, myself as Chairman,\nour neartlest congratulations on the\nhonour conferred upon you by the\nQueen in her Birthday Honour's List.\nIt is indeed gratifying to all\nof us when good work in the public\ninterest is rewarded, and you were\ncertainly deserving of the honour\nbestowed upon you.\nKindest\nwishes,\nregards and best\nours sincerely,\n(P.W. HADDY)\nCHAIRMAN\nC. H. McFadyen, Esq., C.B.E.,\nSepartment of shipping and Transport,\n497 Collins Street.\nMELBOURNE.\nC.1.\nIo have the Honour of Meeting Their Royal Kighnesses The Princess\nElizabeth, Duchess of Edinburgh; and The Duke of Edinburgh\n32\nThe Government of Victoria\nrequests the pleasure of the Company of\nMr and Mrs CH. M-Fadyen\nat a\nFate Reception, at the Exhibition Buildings,\non Wednesday, 26th March, 1952, at 8 odocke p.m.\nAn answer, not later than 20th February,\nis requested to the Secretary, Cabinet Reception Committee,\nPremier's Department. Melbourne, C.2.\nOn receipt of Acceptance,\nEntree Cards will be forwarded.",
